{{was wotd|2009|October|30}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|morbidus||diseased|lang=la}}, from {{term|morbus||sickness|lang=la}}, itself from the root of {{term|morior||die|lang=la}} or directly from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{recons|mor-||to rub, pound, wear away|lang=ine-pro}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈmɔː.bɪd/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈmɔɹ.bɪd/}}
* {{audio|en-us-morbid.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{context|originally|lang=en}} Of, or relating to [[disease]].
# [[unhealthy|Unhealthy]] or [[unwholesome]], especially [[psychologically]]: [[mental illness|mentally ill]]
# Suggesting the [[horror]] of [[death]]; [[macabre]] or [[ghoulish]]
# [[grisly|Grisly]] or [[gruesome]].

====Derived terms====
* [[morbidity]]
* [[morbidly]]
* [[morbidness]]

====Related terms====
* [[morbidezza]]
* [[morbilous]]

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|of or relating to disease}} [[pathological]]
* {{sense|unhealthy or unwholesome}} [[sick]], [[twisted]], [[unhealthy]], [[unwholesome]], [[warped]]
* {{sense|suggesting the horror of death}} [[black]], [[ghoulish]], [[grim]], [[macabre]]
* {{sense|grisly, gruesome}} [[bloody]], [[disgusting]], [[gory]], [[grisly]], [[gruesome]], [[sickening]]

